From: GNS3 appliance maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] package/libvirt: do not force cgroupfs-mount

The appliance uses the unified cgroup v2 hierarchy and Docker Engine.
Buildroot's docker-engine package deliberately conflicts with
cgroupfs-mount, but libvirt 7.10.0 unconditionally selects that legacy
mount helper for non-systemd systems even when only its network driver is
used.

Do not force cgroupfs-mount. The appliance kernel/init setup mounts its
cgroup v2 hierarchy independently, and libvirt is only used to manage the
virbr0 NAT network.

---
 package/libvirt/Config.in | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/package/libvirt/Config.in b/package/libvirt/Config.in
--- a/package/libvirt/Config.in
+++ b/package/libvirt/Config.in
@@ -24,8 +24,6 @@ config BR2_PACKAGE_LIBVIRT
 	select BR2_PACKAGE_LIBTIRPC
 	select BR2_PACKAGE_LIBXML2
 	select BR2_PACKAGE_ZLIB
-	# run-time dependencies
-	select BR2_PACKAGE_CGROUPFS_MOUNT if !BR2_INIT_SYSTEMD
 	help
 	  Libvirt is collection of software that provides a convenient
 	  way to manage virtual machines and other virtualization
